<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lee Kuan Yew</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1923">1923</a>–<a href="/years/2015">2015</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lee Kuan Yew was the first prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, holding office from 1959 to 1990. As leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-action-party">People's Action Party</a> he took Singapore into Malaysia in 1963 and, after its separation in 1965, led it as an independent state. His government built Singapore into a prosperous trading and financial centre under the dominance of a single party.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lee-kuan-yew.jpg" alt="Lee Kuan Yew" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: White House Photographic Office. 1974-1977 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prime_Minister_Lee_Kuan_Yew_of_Singapore_Making_a_Toast_at_a_State_Dinner_Held_in_His_Honor,_1975.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
